## What sorts of Hard/Boring stuff does it automate?

- Versioning and Releasing
- Security and Dependency Updating
- Linting, Styling, and Testing for every Commit and Pull Request
- Publishing Documentation
- License and Policies
- Contribution Guide and Automatic Contributor Crediting

## The Big Decision

There's one big decision to make before you use this template:

- **`project_type`** (Standard or Template): whether the generated project is a finished,
  ready-to-code-in repo (**Standard**), or is a child Copier template that others can build off of in turn (**Template**).

## Inheritance

This template was built from parent template
[{{ parent_template_name }}]({{ parent_template_url }}). Child templates of this template will inherit in the same way. `copier
update` is what keeps that inheritance flowing: run periodically against a generated project, it
pulls in whatever changed upstream (new features, fixes, security patches) without discarding
what's been customized locally.

